hadiths[34]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1262","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Every intoxicating thing is khamr (wine), and every khamr (wine) is forbidden."
"1263","‘Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I received a she-camel as booty on the day of Badr, and on the same day, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave me another she-camel from the khums. Then, when I wished to marry Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her), who was the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I made an agreement with a goldsmith from Banu Qaynuqa‘ that he would go with me and we would both bring idhkhir (a type of grass), and sell it to the goldsmiths, and from that I would arrange the wedding feast for my marriage. I was gathering the equipment for my two she-camels—saddles, stirrups, ropes, etc.—and both she-camels were sitting beside the room of an Ansari. When I finished gathering this equipment and returned, I saw that both she-camels’ humps had been cut off, their bellies ripped open, and their livers taken out. I could not bear to see this, and my eyes could not hold back (that is, I began to weep—not out of worldly greed, but out of the thought of the shortcoming towards Sayyidah Fatimah al-Zahra and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him). I asked, “Who did this?” People said, “Hamzah (may Allah be pleased with him) bin ‘Abd al-Muttalib did it, and he is in that house with a group of the Ansar who are drinking wine. In front of them, and in front of his companions, a singing woman sang a song, in which she said, ‘O Hamzah, get up and deal with these fat she-camels at once.’” Hamzah (may Allah be pleased with him) got up with a sword, cut off their humps, ripped open their bellies, and took out their livers. Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When I heard this, I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), where Zayd bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting. As soon as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw me, he recognized the grief and distress on my face and said, “What has happened to you?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, I have never seen a day like today. Hamzah (may Allah be pleased with him) has wronged my two she-camels, cut off their humps, ripped open their bellies, and he is in that house with a few drunkards.” Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called for his cloak, put it on, and then set out on foot. Zayd bin Harithah and I both followed behind him, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the door where Hamzah (may Allah be pleased with him) was and asked permission to enter. The people gave permission. We saw that they had been drinking wine. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) began to reproach Sayyiduna Hamzah (may Allah be pleased with him) for this action, and Sayyiduna Hamzah’s eyes were red (due to intoxication). He looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then looked at his knees, then raised his gaze to his navel, then raised his gaze to his face, and (being intoxicated) said, “You are nothing but the slaves of my forefathers.” At that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) realized that he was intoxicated, so he turned back and left. We also left with him."
"1264","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came from Jaishan (and Jaishan is a city in Yemen). He asked about the wine of Yemen which was drunk in his country and was made from corn, and it was called Mizr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Does it intoxicate?"" He said, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Whatever intoxicates is forbidden. And Allah Almighty has promised that whoever drinks intoxicants will be made to drink (in the Hereafter) Teenat al-Khabal."" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is Teenat al-Khabal?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""It is the sweat of the inhabitants of Hell, or the blood and pus that comes out of their bodies."
"1265","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about (a type of) wine called ""bat‘"" and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every drink that intoxicates is forbidden."
"1266","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks alcohol in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter, unless he repents."
"1267","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that wine is made from these two trees: one is the date-palm and the other is the grapevine."
"1268","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I was serving wine to Sayyiduna Abu Talha, Abu Dujanah, Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with them), and a group of the Ansar when a person came in and said: ""There is news, wine has been declared unlawful."" Then, on that very day, we poured out the wine, and that wine was made from gudar (i.e., dates whose color had turned red or yellow but were not yet fit to eat) and dried dates. Qatadah said that Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that when wine was prohibited, most of their wine was this khaleet, i.e., made by mixing gudar and dried dates."
"1269","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), praising and glorifying Allah, then said: After praising and glorifying Allah! Know that when wine was made unlawful, it used to be made from five things: wheat, barley, dates, grapes, and honey. And wine is that which clouds the mind (regardless of what it is made from). (By this, the saying of Imam Abu Hanifa is refuted, who said that wine is specific to grapes, because Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said this on the pulpit and all the Companions accepted it, and no one objected, so it became consensus.) O people! I wished that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had explained to us in detail about three things: the inheritance of the grandfather, the inheritance of kalalah, and some chapters regarding usury."
"1270","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) forbade making nabidh by mixing dates and grapes, or by mixing ripe and unripe dates."
"1271","`Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri رضي الله عنه narrates that` the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: Whoever among you drinks nabidh (a drink made from dates or grapes), let him drink only from grapes, or only from dates, or only from dried dates."
"1272","It is narrated from Zadhan, he says: I said to Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), tell me about those things among the drinks from which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade. Explain them in your own language and then clarify them in our language, because your language is a bit different from ours. So he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade (making nabidh) in hantam, that is, earthen jars, in dubba’ (gourd vessels), in muzaffat, that is, pitch-coated vessels, and in naqir, that is, vessels made by hollowing out date-palm wood. And he commanded that nabidh be made in water skins."
"1273","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` Nabidh used to be prepared for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin, and when a waterskin was not available, it was prepared in a stone jar. Some said that I heard from Abu az-Zubair, he used to say that the jar was made of stone."
"1274","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you from (using) vessels, but nothing becomes lawful or unlawful because of vessels, and every intoxicating thing is unlawful."
"1275","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making nabidh in certain vessels, the noble Companions submitted that not all people have access to the vessels in which making nabidh is permitted. So, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) allowed making nabidh in all vessels except for the muzaffat, that is, the oil-coated pitcher."
"1276","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` Nabidh would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the beginning of the night, and he (peace be upon him) would drink it in the morning, then on the second night, then in the morning, then on the third night, then from morning till Asr. After that, whatever remained, he (peace be upon him) would give it to the servant to drink or would order it to be poured away."
"1277","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: We used to soak nabidh (a drink) for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a waterskin and tie a knot in it. There was a hole in it. In the morning we would soak it and at night he (peace be upon him) would drink it, and at night we would soak it and he (peace be upon him) would drink it in the morning."
"1278","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about making vinegar from wine. He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""No."
"1279","It is narrated from Wa'il Hadhrami that Tariq bin Suwaid Jufi (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about wine, so he (peace be upon him) forbade (or disliked) its making. He (Tariq) said: I make it for medicinal purposes. The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: No, it is not a medicine, rather it is a disease."
"1280","Sayyiduna Abu Humayd Sa‘idi (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I brought a bowl of milk from Naqi‘ to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), which was not covered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Why did you not cover it? (If you had nothing to cover it with,) you could have placed a stick across it. Abu Humayd (the narrator of the hadith) says: We were instructed to tie up the water skins and close the doors at night."
"1281","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When night falls, or he said: When you enter the evening, keep your children inside (the houses), for at that time the devils spread out. Then when a part of the night has passed, let them go, and mention the name of Allah and close the doors, for the devil does not open a closed door. And mention the name of Allah when tying the mouth of your water skins, and cover your vessels, mentioning the name of Allah. (If you do not find anything to cover the vessels except to place a stick across them in width, then do so), and extinguish your lamps."
"1282","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Cover the vessels and tie the water skins, for there is a night in the year in which a plague descends. Then, whatever uncovered vessel or untied water skin it finds, the plague descends into it. And in one narration, Laith (the narrator) said that among us, in non-Arab lands, people avoid this in ""Kanun Awwal"" (that is, December)."
"1283","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I have given the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) honey, nabidh, water, and milk to drink from my this cup."
"1284","´Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came from Makkah to Madinah, Suraqah bin Malik (on behalf of the polytheists) pursued him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated against him, so his horse sank (into the ground, meaning the earth seized him). He said, “Pray for me, I will not harm you.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed to Allah (so he was saved). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) felt thirsty and passed by a shepherd of goats. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I took a bowl and milked a little milk for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and brought it to him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) drank it until I was pleased.”"
"1285","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that on the night when the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was taken on the journey to Bayt al-Maqdis, two bowls were brought to him. One contained wine and the other contained milk. He, peace and blessings be upon him, looked at both and chose the bowl of milk. Sayyiduna Jibreel, peace be upon him, said: ""All praise is due to Allah who guided you to the natural disposition (i.e., Islam and steadfastness). If you had chosen the wine, your Ummah would have gone astray."
"1286","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was told about an Arab woman. The Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered Abu Usaid to convey a proposal to her. He conveyed the proposal, and she came and stayed in the forts of Banu Sa’idah. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went out and went to her. When he arrived, he saw a woman with her head lowered. The Prophet (peace be upon him) spoke to her, and she replied, “I seek refuge with Allah from you.” The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, “You have sought protection from me, so I will not say anything to you.” The people said to her, “Do you know who this is?” She said, “No, I do not know.” The people said, “This is the Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s mercy and peace be upon him. He came to speak to you about marriage.” She said, “I was unfortunate (when I sought refuge from you, O Messenger of Allah).” (From this hadith, it is known that it is permissible for a suitor to look at the woman he wishes to marry.) Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came that day and sat with his companions in the Saqifah of Banu Sa’idah, and then said to Sahl, “Serve us a drink.” Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I brought out this cup and served everyone. Abu Hazim said: Sahl brought out that cup, and we also drank from it (for blessing). Then, during his caliphate, Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) asked Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) for that cup, and he gifted it to him."
"1287","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade drinking water directly from the mouth of water-skins by turning them upside down. In another narration, it is mentioned that turning the water-skin upside down means to place its mouth downward and drink directly from it."
"1288","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ukeem says that we were with Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) in Mada’in when he asked for water. A farmer brought water in a silver vessel, so Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) threw the vessel away and said: I am telling you that I had told him not to give me water in a silver vessel, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not drink from gold and silver vessels, and do not wear thick or fine silk, for these things are for (the disbelievers) in this world and for us (Muslims) in the Hereafter on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever drinks from silver vessels is certainly putting the fire of Hell into his belly."
"1289","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks from silver vessels, he is pouring the fire of Hell into his belly. And in another narration: Whoever eats or drinks from gold and silver vessels (he is pouring the fire of Hell into his belly)."
"1290","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to our house and asked for water. We milked a goat and then mixed water from our well into it and gave it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He drank it, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting to his left, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was in front, and on the right side was a Bedouin. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had drunk to his fill, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), pointing towards (Sayyiduna Abu Bakr), said, ""O Messenger of Allah! This is Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave (the remainder) to the Bedouin and did not give to Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), and said, ""Those on the right are given precedence, those on the right, then those on the right."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""This is Sunnah, Sunnah, Sunnah."
"1291","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that a drink was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he drank from it. On his right was a boy and on his left were elderly people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the boy, ""Do you permit me to give it to the elders before you?"" He replied, ""No, by Allah, I do not wish to give up my share to anyone else."" Upon hearing this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed it to the boy."
"1292","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breathing into the vessel."
"1293","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to breathe three times while drinking and used to say that by doing so, one feels satisfied, the thirst is well quenched, or health is restored from illness, and the water is well digested. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that I also breathe three times while drinking water."
"1294","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should drink while standing, and whoever forgetfully does so should vomit it out."
"1295","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` I gave Zamzam water to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he drank it while standing and requested water near the Ka'bah."
